{
  "question": "What additional requirement must a member fulfill to access the laser cutter at the Tide Workshop beyond completing the general induction? Does having a current laser endorsement at the Tide Workshop eliminate the need for a duty steward to be present when using the laser cutter?",
  "expected_status": "answered",
  "expected_facts": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "c4f0ce4a0755cc50",
      "quote": "Laser cutter access requires a separate laser induction and a current equipment endorsement.",
      "source": "membership.md"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "973de2cb039dbd1c",
      "quote": "A current laser endorsement does not waive the steward requirement.",
      "source": "safety.md"
    }
  ],
  "candidate": {
    "status": "answered",
    "answer": "To access the laser cutter at the Tide Workshop beyond completing the general induction, a member must complete a separate laser induction and hold a current laser equipment endorsement. The endorsement expires 12 months after the induction date, and a member with an expired endorsement must attend a refresher before booking the equipment. Having a current laser endorsement does not eliminate the need for a duty steward to be present when using the laser cutter. The policy explicitly states that 'a current laser endorsement does not waive the steward requirement.'",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "chunk_id": "c4f0ce4a0755cc50",
        "quote": "Laser cutter access requires a separate laser induction and a current equipment endorsement. An endorsement expires 12 months after the induction date. A member with an expired endorsement must attend a refresher before booking that equipment."
      },
      {
        "chunk_id": "973de2cb039dbd1c",
        "quote": "A current laser endorsement does not waive the steward requirement. Members must not bypass interlocks, disable guards, or leave running equipment unattended. The assistant must not provide instructions for operating, repairing or bypassing safety systems on any machine. Members should ask the duty steward for equipment-specific guidance."
      }
    ]
  },
  "cited_sources": [
    {
      "id": "c4f0ce4a0755cc50",
      "source": "membership.md",
      "locator": "text",
      "text": "# Tide Workshop membership and access Synthetic demonstration policy. This is not a real workshop or safety standard. Effective 1 October 2026. Applies to adult members at the Riverside site. ## Access The Riverside workshop opens Monday to Friday from 09:00 to 20:00. It opens Saturday from 10:00 to 16:00. The workshop is closed on Sunday. Members must scan their own membership card when entering and leaving. Lending a membership card to another person is not permitted. The minimum membership age is 18 years. ## Induction Every member must complete the general induction before entering a work area. General induction lasts 45 minutes and is booked through the member portal. Completing general induction does not authorize use of the laser cutter. Laser cutter access requires a separate laser induction and a current equipment endorsement. An endorsement expires 12 months after the induction date. A member with an expired endorsement must attend a refresher before booking that equipment. ## Membership and support Standard membership costs INR 900 per month. Membership fees do not include equipment booking fees or materials. Members can",
      "start_word": 0,
      "score": 16.40149
    },
    {
      "id": "973de2cb039dbd1c",
      "source": "safety.md",
      "locator": "text",
      "text": "# Tide Workshop safety and incident reporting Synthetic demonstration policy, not machine operating guidance. Effective 1 October 2026. ## Clothing and protective equipment Closed-toe shoes are required in every work area. Tie back long hair before entering a machine zone. Safety glasses are required in the woodworking zone even when a member is observing. Hearing protection is required when the posted machine notice specifies it. The sewing station does not require safety glasses under this policy. These requirements do not replace machine induction. ## Supervision and prohibited actions The laser cutter may be used only while a duty steward is present in the workshop. A current laser endorsement does not waive the steward requirement. Members must not bypass interlocks, disable guards, or leave running equipment unattended. The assistant must not provide instructions for operating, repairing or bypassing safety systems on any machine. Members should ask the duty steward for equipment-specific guidance. ## Incidents Stop work and notify the duty steward immediately after an injury, equipment fault or near miss. The steward decides whether equipment should be isolated. Submit an incident",
      "start_word": 0,
      "score": 14.79972
    }
  ],
  "tool_results": []
}
